==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|hertely}}, {{m|enm|herteliche}}, {{m|enm|heorteliche}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ġeheortlīċe|t=whole-heartedly, vigorously}}, equivalent to {{suf|en|hearty|ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhɑːtɪli/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhɑɹtɪli/|a=GA}}
* {{hyphenation|en|heart|i|ly}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-heartily.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[hearty]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|eat '''heartily'''}}
#: {{ux|en|greet someone '''heartily'''}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1887|author=Harriet W. Daly|title=Digging, Squatting, and Pioneering Life in the Northern Territory of South Australia|page=166|passage=Sometimes he laughed '''heartily''' as if he heard some capital joke; by degrees this lessened, and he spoke rapidly, but in very low tones.}}

